# A1-S1 (CONDITIONAL, SWAP SPLIT slice 1 of 4, runs when A1-C and its swap re-run both failed to attach): the combined arm with the SDPA audit alone (multi exact against the per-user launches) on the A1-C test set. SMOKE JOBS ONLY: a slice is no audit twin of the
# gates (the three audit-free slices run multi without its audit, which the gates refuse). The four slices together carry exactly the whole audit set of the combined audit twin (test_tp4_w2ln_profiles); all four passing stands in for A1-C, and no audit that only the whole set exercises together is covered.
# A1-C (THE KILL SIGNAL): the COMBINED audited attach (Lever N merged with prefix reuse + multi + F1, every audit, the Lever N digest instrument) on the S0-CTL tests. G-NP0: install lines sticky=1 and "install chunked=levern", the merged warm steps=4,
# route program growth 0, "lever N epoch scope: route writer engaged". G-NP1: every hash equals S0-CTL's, the route ledger clean (levern_route_problems), the digests (slot, logits, KV) equal S0-CTL's by tokens_sha. G-NP4: zero [PACKED-PRESTAGE-FULLAUDIT] mismatches,
# path=diff on at least 95% of rounds after intermediate steps, the shadow ran. W2: "tp4 sdpa engaged config=multi flags=0x21", the multi call line, the UNQUALIFIED line, "conv gates spread engaged gate_cores=2", every audit exact (SDPA exact=True, F1 a multiple of 3 entries a layer).
# AFTER ATTACH read the memory ledger's free DRAM per chip: at least the 600 MB prefill transient plus a margin, before any 254k shape counts (else the POOL SWAP). Fail classes: an F1 audit failure -> F1 SWAP; an SDPA audit failure or a multi refusal -> W2 OUT; a Lever N rule or digest -> LN OUT;
# an attach death on L1, DRAM or trace region -> LEAN or POOL SWAP (ORDER.txt). Before declaring an interaction, run A1-W2 and A1-LN (their test sets are supersets of this one's between them).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the combined development window (docs/tp4-combined-window.md; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w2-levern-prefix and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the classes, the minutes, the NEEDS graph, the swap
# rules and every read and cutover rule. ONE IMAGE FOR THE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2ln-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed branch commit; every window job serves it. The jobs named
# CTL (and T0, G0, E1-CTL) run the PRODUCTION base image tp4-serve-10 (the production engine bytes), driven from this same window commit: the host-side scripts (the smoke shapes, the gates, the kill-switch preflight, the load logger, the raised exactness-shared box) are the window's.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2ln-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-audit-sdpa
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent8_skew,levern_equal,levern_equal_busy,levern_equal_long
